Package: homelab-postfix-block-link
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         homelab-common (>= 0.1.23),
         homelab-postfix,
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         libmojo-pg-perl,
         libsendmail-pmilter-perl,
         adduser,
         sudo
Recommends: homelab-block-link, homelab-domain-admin, homelab-api, homelab-agent
Description: Postfix add-on: injects a click-to-block link into inbound mail
 A Perl Sendmail-Milter-protocol daemon (Sendmail::PMilter), installed
 onto an already-running homelab-postfix host (hard Depends -- this
 package is nothing standalone) and wired into its smtpd_milters/
 non_smtpd_milters chain the same idempotent postconf -e
 read-current-then-append pattern homelab-postfix's own postinst
 already uses for OpenDKIM -- lands after OpenDKIM by construction
 (milters see each other's changes in list order), so OpenDKIM's own
 inbound Authentication-Results verification always reflects the
 untouched original message.
 .
 For each inbound recipient, resolves the envelope address to a
 destination account using the SAME domainadmin.mail_aliases exact-
 then-catch-all lookup Postfix's own routing already does, checks that
 account's click-to-block setting (a per-domain default, per-account
 override -- see homelab-block-link, the companion package that owns
 those settings and the public management page), and if enabled, adds
 a List-Unsubscribe header (and, for domains configured for it, a
 plain-text body footer on unsigned text/plain messages only) pointing
 at a real, unique management link.
 .
 Fails open unconditionally: any database error or unexpected failure
 logs and lets the message through completely unmodified -- this sits
 on the hot SMTP delivery path for every host it's installed on and
 must never become a new way to break core mail delivery.
 .
 Holds its own narrow Postgres role (bespoke bootstrap script, not the
 generic homelab-bootstrap-app-role -- this needs cross-schema grants
 into domainadmin's and homelab-block-link's own schemas, which the
 generic script doesn't produce) with SELECT-only access to alias/
 domain/settings data and INSERT-only access to homelab-block-link's
 own pending_links table. Must be installed AFTER homelab-block-link on
 any given host -- see that package's own README.md "Install order"
 section.
